# What a derived repository does not commit.
#
# Installs as `.gitignore`, overwriting the template's own. Spelled without the dot for
# the same reason as `gitattributes` beside it: `ls sadhana/` is a step in the bootstrap
# skill and a dotfile would not appear in it.
#
# Every rule here is one a repository whose protocols prescribe `git add -A` needs before
# anybody writes a node. That is the organizing principle — this is not a list of build
# output, it is a list of things that appear in a working tree without anyone putting
# them there, in a repository that stages indiscriminately by protocol.

# Runtime configuration.
#
# Both bootstrap and the sangha protocol prescribe `git add -A`. A derived repository was
# found carrying an untracked `.env` that any of those would have staged. It had never
# been committed; the next one may not be so lucky.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Agent worktrees. `.claude/worktrees/<name>` is a git worktree — an embedded repository —
# and `git add -A` stages it as a gitlink pointing at a commit no clone can resolve. Same
# family as the `.env` above.
.claude/worktrees/

# Rust
#
# The yidam binary is installed per-repository rather than into ~/.cargo/bin, so that a
# machine holding several yidam repositories does not run one repo's pinned build against
# another's corpus. `mise run yidam-build` writes it here.
.yidam/bin/
target/
# `cargo --target-dir` output under any name. `target/` alone missed `target-pin/`, which
# a `git add -A` then swept 567 build artifacts out of.
target-*/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
# fastembed downloads its ONNX weights to a cwd-relative directory the first time a model
# is resolved, so `yidam index-build` run from the repository root leaves 23MB of
# untracked model blobs in it.
.fastembed_cache/

